            <ArticleTitle>A Predictable Alternative to a Smile in Six Months?</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>190-2, 195-8</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>The aim of this article is to explore the use of Incognito™ Lite as an alternative to competitors advertising a ‘Smile in Six Months’ or rather short-term orthodontics for improving dental appearance through tooth movement. The focus is on the varied clinical use of this appliance system and its comparative advantages, disadvantages and placement techniques. Some alternatives are discussed and appraised. Two cases successfully treated with Incognito™ Lite are then presented. Clinical relevance: A reliable and predictable tool for aesthetic alignment of teeth, creating a broader range of treatment options for both the clinician and the patient.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
